§ `Civil Liability Act 2003: does the Act reach my claim`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Schedule 2 -- the kinds of harm, and dust-related conditions`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- Sch 2 "harm means harm of any kind, including ... (a) personal injury; (b) damage to property; (c) economic loss."
-- "personal injury includes (a) fatal injury; (b) pre-natal injury; (c) psychological or psychiatric injury; (d)
-- disease." Both "includes" lists: the kinds are offered as choices, with "another kind of harm" left open.
DECLARE `Kind of harm` IS ONE OF
    `personal injury (including death, pre-natal injury, psychological or psychiatric injury, or disease)`
    `damage to property`
    `economic loss`
    `another kind of harm`

-- Sch 2 "dust-related condition means (a) any of the following diseases ... ; or (b) any other pathological condition
-- of the lung, pleura or peritoneum that is attributable to dust." A "means" definition: worked out from the disease
-- named (paragraph (a)) or two facts (paragraph (b)).
DECLARE `Disease or condition` IS ONE OF
    aluminosis
    `asbestos induced carcinoma`
    asbestosis
    `asbestos related pleural diseases`
    bagassosis
    berylliosis
    byssinosis
    `coal dust pneumoconiosis`
    `farmers' lung`
    `hard metal pneumoconiosis`
    mesothelioma
    silicosis
    silicotuberculosis
    talcosis
    `another condition of the lung, pleura or peritoneum`
    `another injury or condition`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A `Disease or condition`
      `attributable to dust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 2 -- a dust-related condition` `the condition` `attributable to dust` IF
    CONSIDER `the condition`
    WHEN `another condition of the lung, pleura or peritoneum` THEN `attributable to dust`
    WHEN `another injury or condition` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 5 -- claims the Act does not decide`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 5(1) "This Act does not apply in relation to deciding liability or awards of damages for personal injury if the
-- harm resulting from the breach of duty is or includes-- (a) an injury for which compensation is payable under the
-- WorkCover Queensland Act 1996, other than an injury to which section 36(1)(c) or 37 of that Act applies; or (b) an
-- injury for which compensation is payable under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003, other than an
-- injury to which section 34(1)(c) or 35 of that Act applies; or (c) ... a dust-related condition; or (d) an injury
-- resulting from smoking or other use of tobacco products or exposure to tobacco smoke."
-- s 5(2): whether compensation is actually claimed, and whether damages are regulated by that Act, is immaterial.
-- s 5(3): the Act still applies "for deciding awards of section 59A damages" for (c) and (d).
-- Whether compensation is payable under a workers' compensation Act, and which of its sections applies, are borrowed:
-- asked as a choice (those Acts are not deposited with this subject).
DECLARE `Workers' compensation for the injury` IS ONE OF
    `no workers' compensation is payable for any of my injuries`
    `compensation is payable under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 for an injury, other than one to which s 34(1)(c) or s 35 of that Act applies`
    `compensation is payable under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 only for an injury to which s 34(1)(c) or s 35 of that Act applies`
    `compensation is payable under the WorkCover Queensland Act 1996 for an injury, other than one to which s 36(1)(c) or s 37 of that Act applies`
    `compensation is payable under the WorkCover Queensland Act 1996 only for an injury to which s 36(1)(c) or s 37 of that Act applies`

DECLARE `Does the Act reach my claim` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Act applies to my claim for damages for harm (s 4(1))`
    `no: the Act does not apply to my personal injury claim, because workers' compensation is payable for an injury (s 5(1)(a) or (b)); whether I claim it is immaterial (s 5(2))`
    `no, except section 59A damages: my injury is or includes a dust-related condition (s 5(1)(c), (3))`
    `no, except section 59A damages: my injury results from smoking or other use of tobacco products or exposure to tobacco smoke (s 5(1)(d), (3))`

GIVEN `the harm` IS A `Kind of harm`
      `workers' compensation` IS A `Workers' compensation for the injury`
      `the condition` IS A `Disease or condition`
      `attributable to dust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Does the Act reach my claim`
`s 5 -- the Act reaches my claim` `the harm` `workers' compensation` `the condition` `attributable to dust` `from tobacco` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the harm` EQUALS `personal injury (including death, pre-natal injury, psychological or psychiatric injury, or disease)`)
        THEN `yes: the Act applies to my claim for damages for harm (s 4(1))`
        IF (`workers' compensation` EQUALS `compensation is payable under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 for an injury, other than one to which s 34(1)(c) or s 35 of that Act applies`)
           OR (`workers' compensation` EQUALS `compensation is payable under the WorkCover Queensland Act 1996 for an injury, other than one to which s 36(1)(c) or s 37 of that Act applies`)
        THEN `no: the Act does not apply to my personal injury claim, because workers' compensation is payable for an injury (s 5(1)(a) or (b)); whether I claim it is immaterial (s 5(2))`
        IF `sch 2 -- a dust-related condition` `the condition` `attributable to dust`
        THEN `no, except section 59A damages: my injury is or includes a dust-related condition (s 5(1)(c), (3))`
        IF `from tobacco`
        THEN `no, except section 59A damages: my injury results from smoking or other use of tobacco products or exposure to tobacco smoke (s 5(1)(d), (3))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the Act applies to my claim for damages for harm (s 4(1))`

@export Does the Civil Liability Act 2003 (Queensland) apply to my claim for damages (ss 4, 5)? It applies to any civil claim for damages for harm, except that for personal injury it does not decide liability or damages where workers' compensation is payable for an injury in the harm (other than an injury to which s 34(1)(c) or s 35 of the 2003 Act, or s 36(1)(c) or s 37 of the 1996 Act, applies), or where the injury is or includes a dust-related condition or results from tobacco; for those two it still decides "section 59A damages" (loss of capacity to care for others).
GIVEN `kind of harm` IS A `Kind of harm` @desc The kind of harm you claim for: personal injury (including death, pre-natal injury, psychological or psychiatric injury, or disease), damage to property, economic loss, or another kind of harm
      `workers compensation` IS A `Workers' compensation for the injury` @desc Whether workers' compensation is payable for any of your injuries from this event, and under which Act; payable means you are entitled to it, whether or not you claimed it
      `condition` IS A `Disease or condition` @desc If your injury is or includes a disease, which one; choose "another condition of the lung, pleura or peritoneum" for any other lung, pleural or peritoneal condition, or "another injury or condition"
      `attributable to dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for "another condition of the lung, pleura or peritoneum": whether the condition is attributable to dust
      `from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury results from smoking or other use of tobacco products, or from exposure to tobacco smoke
GIVETH A `Does the Act reach my claim`
`Does the Act apply to my claim` MEANS
    `s 5 -- the Act reaches my claim` `kind of harm` `workers compensation` `condition` `attributable to dust` `from tobacco`
